msgid "quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:205
msgid "Storing means replacing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:206
msgid "An uploaded JPEG is written out in the new format and the JPEG itself is not kept, so every crop made afterwards — today’s and any made years from now when a size changes — comes out of the converted file rather than out of the camera’s. That is why its quality is set separately here. Setting it higher than the crops is tempting and usually wrong: a copy that comes out larger than the picture it was made from is thrown away, and that picture then gains nothing. On this site’s photographs that happens to 4% of them at 82 and to 22% at 86."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:209
msgid "AVIF is not offered as the stored format on purpose. A handful of browsers still cannot read one, and a picture kept only as AVIF would show them nothing at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:216
#: includes/admin.php:323
msgid "Formats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:230
msgid "quality at 2×"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:237
msgid "The second number is for the double-density sizes — the ones a phone or a Retina screen takes. Those are never drawn at their own size: four of their pixels are averaged into every pixel the eye receives, and an encoder’s artefacts live precisely in the detail that averaging destroys. Compressing them harder is the one saving in this whole business that costs nothing visible. On this site’s photographs it halves the weight of what most visitors actually download."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:241
msgid "The two quality scales are not comparable — they belong to different encoders. The numbers offered here were measured on this site’s own photographs: AVIF at 55 lands around half the weight of the JPEG it came from, WebP at 82 around three quarters. Raising a number makes the copy larger and closer to the original; lowering it does the opposite. Changing either only affects pictures converted afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:248
msgid "Smallest worthwhile saving"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:252
msgid "%"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:255
msgid "A copy that does not come out at least this much smaller than the original is thrown away and not made again. Not every picture compresses: a flat drawing can leave a photographic encoder larger than it went in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:261
msgid "File names"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:267
msgid "Add the extension: picture.jpg.webp"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:273
msgid "Replace the extension: picture.webp"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:277
msgid "Adding is the safe one: the name it is built from was already unique, so the copy cannot collide with anything. Replacing reads better and is what a server-side rewrite rule expects to find, but the day somebody uploads both picture.jpg and picture.png the two copies want the same name. Nothing here needs the rewrite rule — the page tells the browser about the copies itself."
msgstr ""

